  "notes": "Bach BWV 846 Prelude, bars 1-19, ending on the authentic cadence to C (G7 in bar 18 to C in bar 19). Each half-bar: LH bass held for a half note, LH tenor entering a 16th later and held 1.75 beats, RH three-note figure played twice as 16ths. Old repo figuration was not Bach's (missing bass, wrong chords from bar 2). Validation exceptions (intermediate): 16ths are the composer's rhythm; the seconds B3/C4 (bar 8, Cmaj7/B) and E3/F3 (bar 16, Fmaj7/E) are Bach's seventh chords; F#, Bb, Ab, C# are chromatic harmony."
}
